# Backend Architecture

Stack: **Express + Prisma + Socket.io + BullMQ + Zod**

## Layered Architecture

```
Request
  ↓
Routes        → Define endpoints, attach middlewares
  ↓
Validators    → Zod schemas for input validation
  ↓
Controllers   → Handle req/res, delegate to services
  ↓
Services      → Business logic, orchestration
  ↓
Repositories  → Data access, Prisma queries
  ↓
Database      → Prisma Client → PostgreSQL
```

## Folder Responsibilities

| Folder | Responsibility |
|--------|---------------|
| `config/` | Env vars, app config (NEVER hardcode) |
| `constants/` | App-wide constants, enums |
| `controllers/` | HTTP handlers - thin layer |
| `services/` | Business logic - thick layer |
| `repositories/` | DB queries, Prisma wrappers |
| `routes/` | Route definitions |
| `middlewares/` | Auth, error handler, rate limit, upload |
| `validators/` | Zod schemas per route |
| `errors/` | Custom error classes (AppError, NotFoundError, etc) |
| `events/` | EventEmitter listeners (decoupled logic) |
| `jobs/` | BullMQ queues & workers |
| `sockets/` | Socket.io namespaces & handlers |
| `logs/` | Logger setup (Winston/Pino) |
| `types/` | Shared TS types |
| `utils/` | Pure helper functions |
| `database/` | Custom DB scripts, seeders |
| `app.ts` | Express app setup (middlewares, routes) |
| `server.ts` | HTTP + Socket.io server start |

## Controller Pattern
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Thin controller
export const createUser = async (req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {
  try {
    const dto: CreateUserDTO = req.body; // Already validated by middleware
    const user = await userService.create(dto);
    return res.status(201).json({ success: true, data: user });
  } catch (error) {
    next(error); // Forward to error middleware
  }
};

// ❌ BAD: Fat controller with business logic
export const createUser = async (req, res) => {
  const existing = await prisma.user.findUnique({ where: { email: req.body.email } });
  if (existing) return res.status(400).json({ error: 'exists' });
  const hashed = await bcrypt.hash(req.body.password, 10);
  const user = await prisma.user.create({ data: { ...req.body, password: hashed } });
  res.json(user);
};
```

## Service Pattern
```typescript
export class UserService {
  async create(dto: CreateUserDTO): Promise<User> {
    // Business logic
    const existing = await this.repo.findByEmail(dto.email);
    if (existing) throw new ConflictError('Email already in use');

    const hashed = await hashPassword(dto.password);
    const user = await this.repo.create({ ...dto, password: hashed });

    // Emit event for decoupled handlers
    eventEmitter.emit('user.created', user);

    return user;
  }
}
```

## Repository Pattern
```typescript
export class UserRepository {
  constructor(private prisma: PrismaClient) {}

  async findById(id: string): Promise<User | null> {
    return this.prisma.user.findUnique({ where: { id } });
  }

  async create(data: Prisma.UserCreateInput): Promise<User> {
    return this.prisma.user.create({ data });
  }
}
```

## Error Handling
- Use custom error classes from `errors/`
- Always `next(error)` in controllers
- Global error middleware handles all errors

```typescript
// Custom error
export class NotFoundError extends AppError {
  constructor(resource: string) {
    super(`${resource} not found`, 404);
  }
}

// Global handler
app.use((err: Error, req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {
  if (err instanceof AppError) {
    return res.status(err.statusCode).json({ success: false, error: err.message });
  }
  logger.error(err);
  return res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: 'Internal server error' });
});
```

## Validation
- **Always** validate request input với Zod
- Use `validate` middleware in routes

```typescript
import { validate } from '@/middlewares/validate';
import { CreateUserSchema } from '@/validators/user.validator';

router.post('/', validate(CreateUserSchema), userController.create);
```
